  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a single focus group of five participants in one Spanish city, which limits the generalizability of the specific occupational dynamics identified.",
      "what": "This qualitative study analyzed the experiences of five licensed or trainee female taxi drivers in Zaragoza, Spain, using a professionally moderated focus group. The thematic analysis of the transcribed discussions identified seven key themes, including how flexible hours both support caregiving and extend workdays, the concentration of safety risks during night shifts, and the reliance on peer networks and GPS for security.",
      "why": "It documents how female drivers in a medium-sized European city navigate a heavily masculinized occupation, revealing that their physical safety and pregnancy protections remain dependent on informal peer strategies rather than formal, structural policy measures."
    }
  },
